# SolveIK.srv
# Request: target end-effector XYZ (and an optional seed configuration
#          to bias which IK solution/elbow orientation is returned).
# Response: solved joint angles (radians) and whether IK converged.
#
# Referenced by ros/scripts/ik_service_node.py. Place this file in your
# catkin package's srv/ folder and add it to CMakeLists.txt / package.xml
# (add_service_files + generate_messages) so catkin generates the
# SolveIK / SolveIKResponse Python classes that node imports.

geometry_msgs/Point target_xyz
float64[] seed_joint_angles
---
float64[] joint_angles
bool success
